    "INDEX-1<SEP>Why did humans evolve to believe in God?<SEP>The belief in God can be traced back to our ancestors who were seeking answers for the mysteries of the world and the universe. As they observed the natural world and the cosmos, they developed the concept of a higher power or deity to explain the unknown. This belief in a divine being or force provided comfort, guidance, and a sense of purpose in their lives. Over time, these beliefs evolved and diversified into various religions and spiritual practices that continue to shape human culture and society.": -5.53125,
    "INDEX-1<SEP>Why did humans evolve to believe in God?<SEP>Humans evolved to believe in God as a way to make sense of the world and to provide comfort and purpose in life. Belief in a higher power can help individuals cope with the unknown and find meaning in the chaos of existence. Additionally, religion can offer a sense of community and belonging, as well as moral guidance and ethical principles to live by. Ultimately, belief in God is a complex and multifaceted phenomenon that has evolved over time and varies greatly across different cultures and individuals.": -5.78125,
